IMPORT prelude
-- EVERY-EACH-QUANTIFIER-SPEC, phase 2: the other modals, the plain
-- distributive form, and the deadline on the join line.
--
-- A quantified rule with no join line has no continuation either (the checker
-- refuses one without a join), so barrier and fork coincide and what is left
-- is the plain distributive obligation: one obligation per member, all live at
-- once (spec §3.3).

DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF
    Chair    HAS name IS A STRING
    Director HAS name IS A STRING

DECLARE Action IS ONE OF
    Approve HAS who IS AN Actor
    Sublet  HAS who IS AN Actor

theChair MEANS Chair OF "Ms Ng"
a MEANS Director OF "A"
b MEANS Director OF "B"
board MEANS LIST a, b

-- 1. No join line: each director owes an approval by day 10, on their own.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`each approves` MEANS
    EVERY Director d IN board MUST Approve (EXACTLY d) WITHIN 10

#TRACE `each approves` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY a DOES Approve a AT 1
  PARTY b DOES Approve b AT 2

#TRACE `each approves` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY a DOES Approve a AT 1
  PARTY b DOES Approve b AT 20

-- 2. MAY under a barrier. This is the constitutive pattern of spec §2.2.1
--    Pattern B: no director OWES an approval, so nothing is breached when one
--    withholds it — the resolution simply does not pass. Read the second trace
--    carefully: it comes back FULFILLED because nothing was owed, and the
--    HENCE did not fire. A drafter who needs to SEE that the resolution failed
--    writes a LEST on the join.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`the resolution` MEANS
    EVERY Director d IN board MAY Approve (EXACTLY d) WITHIN 30
        ONCE ALL HAVE HENCE FULFILLED

#TRACE `the resolution` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY a DOES Approve a AT 1
  PARTY b DOES Approve b AT 2

#TRACE `the resolution` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY a DOES Approve a AT 1
  PARTY theChair DOES Approve theChair AT 40

-- 3. SHANT under a barrier. A prohibition is kept by NOT acting, so the
--    barrier is achieved when the deadline passes with nobody having sublet.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`no subletting` MEANS
    EVERY Director d IN board SHANT Sublet (EXACTLY d) WITHIN 30
        ONCE ALL HAVE HENCE FULFILLED LEST BREACH

#TRACE `no subletting` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY theChair DOES Approve theChair AT 40

#TRACE `no subletting` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY b DOES Sublet b AT 3
  PARTY theChair DOES Approve theChair AT 40

-- 4. WITHIN in both positions (R-T2). On the act it bounds each approval; on
--    the ONCE line it bounds the whole, so approvals inside their own 30 days
--    still miss if the LAST of them lands after day 10.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`quorum by ten` MEANS
    EVERY Director d IN board MUST Approve (EXACTLY d) WITHIN 30
        ONCE ALL HAVE WITHIN 10 HENCE FULFILLED

#TRACE `quorum by ten` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY a DOES Approve a AT 1
  PARTY b DOES Approve b AT 2

#TRACE `quorum by ten` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY a DOES Approve a AT 1
  PARTY b DOES Approve b AT 20

-- 5. A deadline written ONLY on the join line, under a FORK. It has to bound
--    each act, or nothing would ever expire and the rule could never fail.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`approve, or else` MEANS
    EVERY Director d IN board MUST Approve (EXACTLY d)
        UPON EACH WITHIN 10
        HENCE FULFILLED
        LEST  BREACH BY d

#TRACE `approve, or else` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY a DOES Approve a AT 1
  PARTY b DOES Approve b AT 2

#TRACE `approve, or else` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY a DOES Approve a AT 1
  PARTY theChair DOES Approve theChair AT 500

-- 6. Nesting: a barrier whose HENCE is itself a quantified obligation. The
--    inner rule is armed at the outer join, so its five days run from there.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`then all confirm` MEANS
    EVERY Director d IN board MUST Approve (EXACTLY d) WITHIN 10
        ONCE ALL HAVE
        HENCE (EVERY Director e IN board
                   MUST   Sublet (EXACTLY e)
                   WITHIN 5)

#TRACE `then all confirm` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY a DOES Approve a AT 1
  PARTY b DOES Approve b AT 2
  PARTY a DOES Sublet a AT 3
  PARTY b DOES Sublet b AT 4

#TRACE `then all confirm` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY a DOES Approve a AT 1
  PARTY b DOES Approve b AT 2
  PARTY a DOES Sublet a AT 3
  PARTY b DOES Sublet b AT 9
